citations.review_text:
One of the best sequels for a game. Period. It took what Asylum already had and it made it 10x better. A bigger map to explore, improved combat to counter enemies already existing in the previous game and slightly much more variety of enemies, much more expanded Batman lore and a well done and written story (on par with Origins, if not slightly below Origins) and more impactful than Asylum (not that Asylum' story is bad), plus the larger number of challenges, more playable characters and the addition of side missions AND a small DLC.

Now I wanna rank the Batman Arkham games based on my preference (you can laugh at me if you want):
1. A. Origins (it has its big issues in some areas but if the game had a whole remaster and a small rework, then it would have been of par with City, if not better);
2. A. Asylum (the game that started the whole series and it should be praised more);
3. A. Knight (some writing regarding Jason Todd, some side missions that were lacking and the slight overuse of the batmobile kinda ruined the experience for me + some other nitpicks but this is still the best looking game from the series and for gaming in general);
4. A. City (yep, still not my favorite even when I 100% the game, probably because of both Riddler trophies and challenges AND because of some performance issues which I never, ever had with the other games, even Origins).
 
It highly deserves its GOTY title for its many improvements, and it's THE game that sequels should take lessons from but personally if I had to replay a Batman Arkham game, City would not be the first on my mind.

